Personally, I couldn't care less if people cheated while playing Nethack;
I've done it before.  Who does it harm?  And anyone who complains about it
is not thinking about why they are playing the game.  Are they playing it
for their own enjoyment, or just to beat everyone else...  They should be
competing with themselves, not others, to see if they can beat their
personal best.  To this end, it may be a good idea if when a character dies,
and the results table comes up, only their _own_ scores are shown.

I find it intensely frustrating that the game does not allow you to make
backups like most other games do.  I have played probably more than two
hundred games, and every time, something really annoying happens on the first
few levels...

Like the newt who bites me on the toe and kills me instantantly.  Or the box
that visciously takes my life when I'm trying to boot it open (I haven't
noticed how few hit-points I have left.

When I really pay as much attention as I can, I can usually get down to about
level five, then I die of lack of food (even when conserving moves).  I have
been reading rec.games.hack for a while now, and I really want to be able to
get further into the game.  Level six is the furthest I have been.  Is there
something I am doing wrong?  I normally play a wizard, because I like that
class.  I know that they should be slightly harder to play because they can
use magic, but are any other classes much easier?  I have played priests and
barbarians, but I still have these problems.  Can anyone help?

I don't want no flames from no elite hack-players, 'cos people who complain
about others taking all their glory are probably self-centred egoist/egotists
who are obsessed with getting a better score that everyone else.  (Great, you
can really play the game well, be proud of yourself, don't put others down
because they're not as good as you).

Fish.
